Wireframes Reflection

The desktop and phone layouts are different mostly because the desktop has way more space. On the desktop version, I can have more buttons and information on the screen without covering up the game. The phone version needs bigger buttons because the player has to tap them with their fingers.

I moved and resized some of the HUD elements for the phone version. The movement and attack buttons are bigger and closer to the bottom of the screen so they are easier to reach. I also kept some of the less important information smaller so it doesn't take up too much space.

I noticed that designing for real screen sizes is harder than I thought because there isn't unlimited space. Something that looks fine on a big screen can cover up half the game on a phone. I had to think about where the player would actually be looking and what buttons they would need.

The player's experience would be a little different between the two versions. The desktop version would have more information visible at once and would probably be easier to control with a keyboard and mouse. The phone version would be more focused on large touch buttons and keeping the screen from getting too crowded.
